    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7593" root="حرد" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَرْدٌ</span></b>  <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَصْدٌ</span>: whence the phrase, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَدْ حَرَدْتُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَرْدَكَ</span>: see 1. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>Anger;</i> [as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَرَدٌ</span></b> : see 1:]
so in the prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَسَّكْ بِحَرْدِكَ حَتَّى تُدْرِكَ حَقَّكَ</span>
<i>Retain,</i> or <i>persist in, thine anger until thou obtain thy right.</i> (TA.) <i>Rancour,</i> or <i>enmity which
one retains in the heart, watching for an opportunity to indulge it.</i> (El-Kálee, MF.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  See
also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَرِيدٌ</span>.

